  "BIOLOGY": "Metaplasticity / BCM sliding threshold (Lee & Kirkwood 2019, Front Cell Neurosci 13:520, DOI:10.3389/fncel.2019.00520): a companion process that adjusts the threshold for plasticity from a unit's OWN recent activity history, rather than one fixed bound shared by every unit. Realized here as a per-seed LIVE safety ceiling discovered from that seed's own coincidence-output trajectory (a local-derivative abrupt-cliff check plus a sustained-decline check, both sized from the parent build's own already-measured dip/cliff magnitudes), generalizing the parent live homeostat's single global constant ceiling into a genuinely per-unit, activity-dependent bound."
